*2. Three Building Blocks of Algorithms
All algorithms are built from these 3 structures:
a. Sequence
Steps executed one after another in order.
_Example: _Making tea
1. Boil water
2. Put tea bag in cup
3. Pour hot water
4. Remove tea bag
b. Selection (IF/ELSE)
Make a decision and choose a path based on a condition.
_Example:_ Checking if you have an umbrella
IF it is raining THEN
    Take umbrella
ELSE
    Go without umbrella
END IF
c. Iteration (Loops)
Repeat a set of steps until a condition is met.
_Example:_ Counting to 5
SET count = 1
WHILE count <= 5 DO
    PRINT count
    Count = count + 1
END WHILE
